asr-000781
01:20:39.900 --> 01:20:42.180
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: has to be the highest budgetary

asr-000782
01:20:42.180 --> 01:20:43.100
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: allocation,

asr-000783
01:20:43.460 --> 01:20:45.840
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: it's actually beneficial to our countrymen.

asr-000784
01:20:47.760 --> 01:20:49.060
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Then, Madam Speaker,

asr-000785
01:20:49.620 --> 01:20:51.820
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: when Congress

asr-000786
01:20:51.820 --> 01:20:53.860
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: evaluates this bill, shouldn't we look

asr-000787
01:20:53.860 --> 01:20:55.640
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: not merely on whether education

asr-000788
01:20:55.640 --> 01:20:57.620
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: receives the largest

asr-000789
01:20:57.620 --> 01:20:59.720
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: nominal amount, but whether

asr-000790
01:20:59.720 --> 01:21:01.860
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: our overall fiscal choices

asr-000791
01:21:01.860 --> 01:21:04.800
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: preserve constitutional priorities

asr-000792
01:21:04.800 --> 01:21:06.660
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: given to education

asr-000793
01:21:06.660 --> 01:21:08.100
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: despite

asr-000794
01:21:08.100 --> 01:21:10.460
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: rising automatic obligation?

asr-000795
01:21:13.460 --> 01:21:14.680
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Madam Speaker,

asr-000796
01:21:14.860 --> 01:21:15.580
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: distinguished colleague,

asr-000797
01:21:15.960 --> 01:21:18.440
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: yes, I agree with

asr-000798
01:21:18.440 --> 01:21:19.440
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: our distinguished colleague.

asr-000799
01:21:20.020 --> 01:21:21.900
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: However, when we look at the budget

asr-000800
01:21:21.900 --> 01:21:23.960
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: and we determine

asr-000801
01:21:23.960 --> 01:21:26.800
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: the allocations

asr-000802
01:21:26.800 --> 01:21:28.000
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: for the different agencies,

asr-000803
01:21:28.000 --> 01:21:29.700
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: we look at it at a holistic level.

asr-000804
01:21:29.720 --> 01:21:31.960
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: But, yes, I agree, Madam Speaker.

asr-000805
01:21:33.060 --> 01:21:33.700
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Madam Speaker,

asr-000806
01:21:33.840 --> 01:21:35.540
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: I raised this question because

asr-000807
01:21:35.540 --> 01:21:37.880
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: comparison between

asr-000808
01:21:37.880 --> 01:21:39.760
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: the interest payment

asr-000809
01:21:39.760 --> 01:21:41.980
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: and the budget

asr-000810
01:21:41.980 --> 01:21:42.860
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: for DepEd

asr-000811
01:21:42.860 --> 01:21:46.720
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: is 1.114 trillion

asr-000812
01:21:46.720 --> 01:21:48.000
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: for interest payments

asr-000813
01:21:48.000 --> 01:21:49.560
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: and

asr-000814
01:21:49.560 --> 01:21:51.840
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: 976 billion

asr-000815
01:21:51.840 --> 01:21:53.780
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: for the Department

asr-000816
01:21:53.780 --> 01:21:54.460
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: of Education.

asr-000817
01:21:55.920 --> 01:21:56.880
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Madam Speaker,

asr-000818
01:21:56.880 --> 01:21:58.780
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: would the sponsor

asr-000819
01:21:58.780 --> 01:21:59.260
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: agree?

asr-000820
01:21:59.720 --> 01:22:01.520
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: That, as a general rule,

asr-000821
01:22:02.580 --> 01:22:04.580
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Congress should prepare

asr-000822
01:22:04.580 --> 01:22:07.240
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: specific itemized appropriations

asr-000823
01:22:07.240 --> 01:22:09.720
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: over broad lump sums

asr-000824
01:22:09.720 --> 01:22:11.780
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: whenever the expenditure

asr-000825
01:22:11.780 --> 01:22:13.940
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: can reasonably be identified

asr-000826
01:22:13.940 --> 01:22:14.760
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: in advance?

asr-000827
01:22:16.660 --> 01:22:17.720
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Yes, Madam Speaker,

asr-000828
01:22:18.100 --> 01:22:19.400
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: distinguished colleague, I agree.

asr-000829
01:22:19.920 --> 01:22:22.160
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Where possible, we would prefer

asr-000830
01:22:22.160 --> 01:22:24.720
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: specific line items over lump sum amounts.

asr-000831
01:22:26.060 --> 01:22:26.800
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Thank you, Madam Speaker,

asr-000832
01:22:26.800 --> 01:22:27.620
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: for that answer.

asr-000833
01:22:28.040 --> 01:22:28.980
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: But, Madam Speaker,

asr-000834
01:22:29.720 --> 01:22:31.260
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: there are items

asr-000835
01:22:31.260 --> 01:22:32.860
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: which we cannot really calculate.

asr-000836
01:22:33.620 --> 01:22:35.700
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Example, calamities.

asr-000837
01:22:36.540 --> 01:22:37.300
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: We shall have

asr-000838
01:22:37.300 --> 01:22:39.600
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: leeway for that.

asr-000839
01:22:41.940 --> 01:22:43.660
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: It cannot be predicted.

asr-000840
01:22:43.920 --> 01:22:45.420
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: But roads, bridges,

asr-000841
01:22:46.640 --> 01:22:47.600
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: buildings, and other

asr-000842
01:22:47.600 --> 01:22:50.080
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: identified infrastructure

asr-000843
01:22:50.080 --> 01:22:52.200
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: normally can be.

asr-000844
01:22:53.540 --> 01:22:54.320
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Can the sponsor

asr-000845
01:22:54.320 --> 01:22:55.880
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: therefore assure the House

asr-000846
01:22:55.880 --> 01:22:57.800
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: that broad lump sums

asr-000847
01:22:57.800 --> 01:22:58.580
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: have not simply been

asr-000848
01:22:58.580 --> 01:23:00.940
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: migrated from

asr-000849
01:23:00.940 --> 01:23:02.620
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: unprogrammed appropriations

asr-000850
01:23:02.620 --> 01:23:04.980
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: into programmed appropriations

asr-000851
01:23:04.980 --> 01:23:06.460
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: or special provision?

asr-000852
01:23:21.000 --> 01:23:22.020
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Thank you, Madam Speaker.

asr-000853
01:23:22.040 --> 01:23:22.800
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Distinguished colleague,

asr-000854
01:23:23.140 --> 01:23:25.080
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: with regard to that particular instance,

asr-000855
01:23:25.740 --> 01:23:27.660
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: in response to the calamities,

asr-000856
01:23:27.780 --> 01:23:28.260
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: we do have

asr-000857
01:23:28.260 --> 01:23:44.000
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: the NDRRMF, which at the moment has an allocation of 45.67 billion. While that is a lump sum amount, we do have within it QRF allocations for the different agencies.

asr-000858
01:23:44.000 --> 01:24:04.540
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: In that case, given that it needs to be flexible to be able to respond to whichever agencies, calamities, or activities would need to be funded at a particular time, for this particular instance, a lump sum amount is actually preferable for the NDRRMF.

asr-000859
01:24:07.540 --> 01:24:09.620
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Thank you for that, Madam Speaker.

asr-000860
01:24:10.420 --> 01:24:16.480
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Because our country is most often visited by typhoons and catastrophes.

asr-000861
01:24:18.080 --> 01:24:34.180
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Would the sponsor agree that a special provision should implement an appropriation approved by Congress and should not effectively create a new spending authority that is broader than the appropriation itself?

asr-000862
01:24:44.000 --> 01:24:57.000
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague, a special provision sets the condition by which an appropriation can be disbursed.

asr-000863
01:24:58.100 --> 01:25:02.240
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So, a special provision emanates from the appropriation itself.

asr-000864
01:25:02.440 --> 01:25:09.960
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So, in theory, technically speaking, a special provision would not supersede a particular appropriation.

asr-000865
01:25:09.960 --> 01:25:13.960
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: And this conforms to our Constitution and applicable law.

asr-000866
01:25:14.000 --> 01:25:15.000
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Madam Speaker.

asr-000867
01:25:15.000 --> 01:25:17.000
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Yes, Madam Speaker.

asr-000868
01:25:17.000 --> 01:25:35.340
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Then, can the sponsor assure this Chamber that there is no provision in this bill that allows funds appropriated for one clearly defined purpose to be redirected to an unrelated purpose without returning to Congress?

asr-000869
01:26:07.000 --> 01:26:10.480
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague, in general, that is the case.

asr-000870
01:26:10.480 --> 01:26:13.480
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: However, there is a general provision within the

asr-000871
01:26:14.000 --> 01:26:22.440
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: General Appropriations Bill which allows for the declaration and use of savings, which is guided by Supreme Court jurisprudence.

asr-000872
01:26:22.440 --> 01:26:40.600
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: But generally, aside from that particular case, generally, whichever intended use is there when the GAA was approved should be eventually the use for a particular fund.

asr-000873
01:26:44.000 --> 01:26:59.260
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Madam Speaker, we can also probably revisit on augmentation, on fund transfers, on GOCC remittances, foreign assisted fund projects, lump sum infrastructure,

asr-000874
01:27:00.860 --> 01:27:05.020
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: LGU support funds, and release of unprogrammed appropriations.

asr-000875
01:27:05.280 --> 01:27:06.140
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Madam Speaker.

asr-000876
01:27:22.000 --> 01:27:24.280
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Madam Speaker, my apologies.

asr-000877
01:27:24.280 --> 01:27:32.300
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: May I clarify if there is a question from the Honorable Minority Leader, or is it more of an example of the different kinds of funds?

asr-000878
01:27:32.300 --> 01:27:39.100
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: It's just to revisit like your assurance that the Madam Sponsor gave us about the use of savings.

asr-000879
01:27:40.480 --> 01:27:43.480
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Perhaps we can revisit the appropriate

asr-000880
01:27:44.000 --> 01:27:51.700
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: laws on this so that, if possible, we go back to Congress for appropriation.

asr-000882
01:28:50.000 --> 01:29:02.100
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague, after consultation with DBM, for those particular items, generally it is governed by the general provision on the Declaration and Use of Savings.

asr-000883
01:29:02.100 --> 01:29:16.080
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: However, upon conferring with the DBM, what they can assure is that they will make sure that they will strictly adhere to whichever conditions are there that is set forth in the general provision for the use of savings.

asr-000884
01:29:16.080 --> 01:29:32.080
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So there will, because that particular general provision is also authorized by Congress, but what they can assure, what the DBM can assure is that those funds will not be reallocated.

asr-000885
01:29:32.100 --> 01:29:41.420
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: They will not be reallocated or augmented without adherence to the particular conditions set forth in the general provision.

asr-000886
01:29:43.280 --> 01:29:45.320
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Thank you for that assurance, Madam Speaker.

asr-000887
01:29:45.800 --> 01:29:59.720
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: Madam Speaker, of the 7.2 trillion before us, how much is truly discretionary and how much is already committed by automatic appropriations, statutory transfers?

asr-000888
01:30:00.000 --> 01:30:03.200
Minority Leader Marcelino C. Libanan: personal obligations, and debt service.

asr-000889
01:30:04.780 --> 01:30:07.000
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague,

asr-000890
01:30:07.120 --> 01:30:10.440
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: in terms of the split for the 7.2 trillion pesos,

asr-000891
01:30:11.140 --> 01:30:15.280
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: 4.494 trillion is under programmed appropriations

asr-000892
01:30:15.280 --> 01:30:20.420
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: and 2.706 trillion is under automatic appropriations.

asr-000893
01:30:21.060 --> 01:30:23.280
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So on the part of Congress,

asr-000894
01:30:24.280 --> 01:30:26.480
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: in the General Appropriations Bill,

asr-000895
01:30:26.480 --> 01:30:29.180
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: we are unable to touch the automatic appropriations.

asr-000896
01:30:29.180 --> 01:30:33.980
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So we are looking at the 4.494 trillion pesos

asr-000897
