asr-005190
05:48:31.440 --> 05:48:35.960
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: 2026 ay naisagawa nila,

asr-005191
05:48:36.220 --> 05:48:36.720
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker.

asr-005192
05:48:37.460 --> 05:48:39.300
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Tama po, Madam Speaker, distinguished colleague,

asr-005193
05:48:39.420 --> 05:48:41.280
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: for them to be considered a cleared

asr-005194
05:48:41.280 --> 05:48:43.440
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: barangay for inclusion in the

asr-005195
05:48:43.440 --> 05:48:45.640
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: 2027 NEP, kailangan

asr-005196
05:48:45.640 --> 05:48:47.860
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: po na gawa po nila

asr-005197
05:48:47.860 --> 05:48:49.580
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: yung CSP at retooled CSP

asr-005198
05:48:49.580 --> 05:48:51.620
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: ng calendar year 2026.

asr-005199
05:48:52.000 --> 05:48:53.580
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Saan po nakalista, Madam Speaker,

asr-005200
05:48:53.720 --> 05:48:55.700
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: good sponsor, kung ano pong listahan

asr-005201
05:48:55.700 --> 05:48:57.860
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: ng mga community support programs na ito?

asr-005202
05:48:59.980 --> 05:49:18.000
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Because Madam Speaker, even the answer just that dapat naka-undergo sila ng CSPs still puts into question ano po ba siya and hindi pa nakukomplete yung answer kung ano po ba yung criteria na ito, Madam Speaker.

asr-005203
05:49:18.000 --> 05:49:40.120
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague, we're just looking at it kasi sa special provision po ng NTF-LCAC, meron ng mga qualified programs under CSP. So may menu din po yung CSP. We're just looking for it po as a special provision to NTF-LCAC.

asr-005204
05:49:40.680 --> 05:49:41.440
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Thank you, Madam Speaker.

asr-005205
05:49:41.440 --> 05:49:44.780
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Please give us a few seconds, Madam Speaker, Distinguished Colleague.

asr-005206
05:49:48.000 --> 05:49:49.000
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: ...

asr-005207
05:50:18.000 --> 05:50:43.640
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Colleague, my apologies. I would like to clarify my answer earlier. So ang nagsasagawa po ng CSP is DILG. So they conduct the community support program with the different target beneficiary barangays in order for them to determine which of the projects are best suited for that particular barangay.

asr-005208
05:50:43.640 --> 05:50:47.740
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Tapos yung particular menu po na yun.

asr-005209
05:50:48.000 --> 05:51:01.660
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Yun yung farm-to-market roads, school building, water and sanitation system, health stations, and electrification. So the whole process of conducting the CSP lies with DILG po. Wala pong visibility yung DBM.

asr-005210
05:51:02.800 --> 05:51:17.900
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, good sponsor, na-mention nga po kung ano yung mga CSPs na yun lang po dapat yung saklaw ng BDP. However, sa website po ng NTF-LCAC kung saan pwede pong ilista.

asr-005211
05:51:18.000 --> 05:51:47.120
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Yung mga BDPs na naimplementa, meron din daw housing or reconstruction at livelihood projects without breakdown of which barangays implemented what. It therefore begs the question, Madam Speaker, good sponsor, saan-saan nga ba napunta ang pondo na ito? Natatapos ba ang mga proyekto na ito sa ilalim ng BDP? O tulad ba ito ng ghost or substandard projects na natimbog po natin last year?

asr-005212
05:51:48.000 --> 05:52:14.280
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Madam Speaker, distinguished colleague, the report as to where the funds went and what programs or projects each barangay got is actually being generated and maintained po by DILG. And that particular report is available in their Subay Bayan portal. So may full list po ng lahat po ng mga projects na napondohan under NTF-LCAC.

asr-005213
05:52:14.280 --> 05:52:15.680
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Yes po, Madam Speaker.

asr-005214
05:52:18.000 --> 05:52:44.180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Sa website, there are items there that are not provided for in that special provision or in the classification of CSPs. As I mentioned po, there's housing, there's reconstruction, and it is not contemplated in the list provided by the good sponsor which said that may form to market roads, school building, water and sanitation system, health stations, and electrification.

asr-005215
05:52:44.180 --> 05:52:47.980
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So saan po nanggaling yung ibang mga items na ito?

asr-005216
05:52:48.000 --> 05:53:07.080
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And ano yung role po ng DBM or ng DBCC to ensure na kung ano lang po yung nakalagay sa special provision, yun po yung na-implementa? Kung meron pong nakalista na hindi po nasa loob ng CSP, ano pong karampatang aksyon ang magawa para po macheck kung tama po yung funding?

asr-005217
05:53:07.400 --> 05:53:12.220
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Thank you very much po for bringing up that point, Madam Speaker, distinguished colleague.

asr-005218
05:53:12.780 --> 05:53:17.780
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Actually, nabanggit din po ng DBM yun na yung monitoring po.

asr-005219
05:53:18.000 --> 05:53:35.640
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Kapat ay nasa DILG, reporting sa kanila. But also, it should be part of the COA audit report. Kung may nakita po na mga proyekto na na-implement na wala po doon sa menu na sinet, kailangan po makall yung attention.

asr-005220
05:53:35.640 --> 05:53:46.860
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So thank you very much po to our distinguished colleague for bringing that up. We can relay that also to DILG and COA to look into these items po.

asr-005221
05:53:46.860 --> 05:54:15.500
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: But to clarify, thank you for answering that. If ever there is feedback on that, Madam Speaker, good sponsor, if it can be written, this representation would like a copy of the feedback kung ano pong explanation kung bakit may ganitong mga items listed sa website na wala naman po sa mga nalistang CSPs. If that's possible, Madam Speaker, good sponsor.

asr-005222
05:54:15.500 --> 05:54:35.600
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Yes, Madam Speaker, distinguished colleague. That would be possible. We'll just have to coordinate with COA and DILG with regard to that. Because as of now po, as per DBM, wala po pong nare-receive na report yung DBM with regard to this. So once available po, we'll share it with our distinguished colleague.

asr-005223
05:54:35.700 --> 05:54:45.480
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: But to clarify, Madam Speaker, good sponsor, kapag sabi ng barangay na ito ay nasa ilalim or naisip,

asr-005224
05:54:45.500 --> 05:55:12.260
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: na isagawa yung CSP and therefore they can qualify for funding ng BDP for 2027, ano po ang therefore nakukuha ng DBM para po ma-authorize na sila po ay pwedeng makakuha ng funding ulit for BDP? It's just a list of barangays? Is that the limitation of the visibility of DBM, Madam Speaker, good sponsor?

asr-005225
05:55:15.500 --> 05:55:45.300
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Yes, Madam Speaker, distinguished colleague. Even though they're listed separately already in the GAA, at the point of release, kailangan po ulit magsumite ng DILG sa DBM ng patunay. Essentially, they endorse which of the qualified barangays actually already went the CSP and meron ng identified project and plansyado na po lahat ng requirements.

asr-005226
05:55:45.500 --> 05:55:50.940
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: And only then will DBM release the funding for that particular project.

asr-005227
05:55:51.140 --> 05:56:15.380
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: We raise these questions, Madam Speaker, good sponsor, because the NTF-ELCAC, since its establishment and has also been notorious in its reputation internationally, it targets unarmed civilians, progressives, and activists. Kahit po igiit na issued by the DBM in coordination with the NTF-ELCAC and limited po ang visibility ng DBM,

asr-005228
05:56:15.500 --> 05:56:33.080
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: sa certifications in relation to BDM funds na wala rin pong nahawakan na pera ang NTF-ELCAC mismo, it is upon us as the branch of government with the power of the purse to question where the budget goes.

asr-005229
05:56:33.080 --> 05:56:45.420
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Hindi natin kinakwestiyon ng pag-unlad o grassroots development. We actually want that, Madam Speaker, good sponsor. What we do not want is conditional development that the BDP of the NTF-ELCAC shows.

asr-005230
05:56:45.500 --> 05:56:49.560
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: O kailangan cleared ka muna bago ka makakakuha ng pondo.

asr-005231
05:56:49.980 --> 05:57:00.000
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And this representation will move at the proper time to amend the HGAB for the abolition of the BDP and the transferring of the funding directly to schools, housing, and the like.

asr-005232
05:57:00.000 --> 05:57:13.600
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Because this representation, Madam Speaker, good sponsor, is not convinced that the scheme that is being implemented now, wherein DBM has limited visibility para macheck pong ano pong effectivity,

asr-005233
05:57:13.600 --> 05:57:31.240
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: and even yung qualification ng CSP supposedly na nakuha ng previous barangay cleared that entitles them to funding now, should allow for more billions to be funneled in this way.

asr-005234
05:57:31.640 --> 05:57:36.040
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Kung pwede naman pong nakaayon po ito sa master plan, Madam Speaker, good sponsor.

asr-005235
05:57:36.960 --> 05:57:41.520
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, good sponsor, if there's no response, I'd like to move on to my next line of questioning.

asr-005236
05:57:41.520 --> 05:57:42.520
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker.

asr-005237
05:57:43.600 --> 05:57:47.100
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, good sponsor, this is now about confidential funds.

asr-005238
05:57:47.940 --> 05:57:55.360
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Article 2, Section 28 of the 1987 Constitution says that subject to reasonable conditions prescribed by law,

asr-005239
05:57:55.900 --> 05:58:03.440
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: the state adopts and implements a policy of full public disclosure of all its transactions involving public interest.

asr-005240
05:58:03.960 --> 05:58:11.400
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: While Article 3, Section 7 states the right of the people to information on matters of public concern shall be recognized.

asr-005241
05:58:11.860 --> 05:58:13.400
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: However, the General Assembly...

asr-005242
05:58:13.600 --> 05:58:26.320
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: The General Principles and Provisions of House Bill 10585 again authorize lump sum confidential and intelligence appropriations across various agencies of the national government.

asr-005243
05:58:26.320 --> 05:58:39.300
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And under Joint Circular No. 2015-01 between DBMs, COA, and other agencies, disbursements from these funds are supported by documentary evidence kept in sealed envelopes.

asr-005244
05:58:39.860 --> 05:58:43.520
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Liquidation is subjected only to post-audit by the COA.

asr-005246
05:58:43.580 --> 05:58:50.060
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: The COA Intelligence and Confidential Fund Audit Unit and a notice of this allowance may be issued years after the fact.

asr-005247
05:58:50.600 --> 05:59:01.400
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: A delay now glaringly exposed as the impeachment proceedings reveal questionable confidential fund disbursements that escape timely scrutiny.

asr-005248
05:59:02.320 --> 05:59:12.600
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Can the sponsor therefore explain the wisdom of retaining confidential fund provisions in the 2027 GAB and its general principles

asr-005249
05:59:12.600 --> 05:59:13.500
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: when the existing...

asr-005250
05:59:13.500 --> 05:59:25.760
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: When the existing audit architecture inherently guarantees that illegal or unconstitutional spending can remain concealed for years, defeating the constitutional demand for public accountability, Madam Speaker?

asr-005251
05:59:43.500 --> 05:59:57.600
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: When the existing audit architecture inherently guarantees that illegal or unconstitutional spending can remain concealed for years, defeating the constitutional demand for public accountability, Madam Speaker?

asr-005252
05:59:57.600 --> 06:00:00.020
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Mr. Speaker, Distinguished Colleague, the...

asr-005253
06:00:00.000 --> 06:00:26.680
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: The basis for essentially which outlines the guidelines for allotment of confidential intelligence funds or essentially outlines who are allowed to avail of confidential intelligence funds is outlined in the COA, DBM, DILG, GECG, and DND Joint Circular Number 2015-01.

asr-005254
06:00:26.680 --> 06:00:45.960
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So there, in Section 4.0, it says that the following are entitled to confidential funds and intelligence funds. So kung iisa-isahin po ba natin, there are…

asr-005255
06:00:45.960 --> 06:00:53.920
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, good sponsor, perhaps no need for that because the good secretary already did that during the budget briefing.

asr-005256
06:00:53.920 --> 06:00:55.920
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: But I am asking, Madam Speaker…

asr-005257
06:00:56.680 --> 06:01:12.840
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: For the wisdom of the continuing grant of confidential expenses, despite the exposure of the currently flawed architecture that allows the disbursement of confidential expenses,

asr-005258
06:01:12.840 --> 06:01:23.040
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: but when there are illegal or abusive expenses, it can take years before it can be exposed,

asr-005259
06:01:23.820 --> 06:01:25.840
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: which by then, lumabas.

asr-005260
06:01:26.680 --> 06:01:34.520
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Lumabas na yung funding. Sana na po napunta sa ibang mas deserving na items, but nonetheless, ay pinunta po sa confidential funds.

asr-005261
06:01:35.000 --> 06:01:41.780
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: This is the topic of the daily political diet of Filipinos. Bakit may confidential funds?

asr-005262
06:01:42.320 --> 06:01:48.820
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So we have an opportunity to engage it in this budget, but it's still here, Madam Speaker, good sponsor.

asr-005263
06:01:49.820 --> 06:01:55.820
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Madam Speaker, distinguished colleague, if you would look at the NEP,

asr-005264
06:01:56.680 --> 06:02:07.540
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: the 2027 NEP, yung whichever agencies had COA findings relating to their confidential and intelligence funds,

asr-005265
06:02:07.660 --> 06:02:13.480
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: wala pong inalocate na CIF sa loob po na 2027 NEP.

asr-005266
06:02:13.480 --> 06:02:26.480
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: The agencies that were given continuing confidential or intelligence funds are those that really have mandates relating to national security.

asr-005267
06:02:26.680 --> 06:02:45.000
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So, doon po sa ating budget, ang meron lang po is DOF, BOC, DILG-OSEC, DILG-PNP, DOJ-OSEC, DOJ-NBI, AMLAC, ARTA, DND, and DOTR.

asr-005268
06:02:45.000 --> 06:02:54.500
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So, and the Office of the President.

asr-005269
06:02:54.500 --> 06:02:56.620
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So, yun lang po. Linimitahan naman na po.

asr-005270
06:02:56.680 --> 06:03:05.000
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So, yung bilang ng mga ahensya, sinigurado po ng DBM sa pagbuo po ng 2027 NEP,

asr-005271
06:03:05.160 --> 06:03:10.860
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: natangin yung mga ahensya lang po talaga na may mandato na related po sa,

asr-005272
06:03:11.100 --> 06:03:16.300
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: na pwede pong lagyan ng kaukalang CIF yung kanila po ninagyan sa budget.

asr-005273
06:03:17.800 --> 06:03:22.420
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: And no increase po, sorry. Much lower than it was in the previous year.

asr-005274
06:03:22.420 --> 06:03:24.160
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, good sponsor.

asr-005275
06:03:24.160 --> 06:03:31.220
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, perhaps we still need to sharply interrogate whose security is actually being served

asr-005276
06:03:31.220 --> 06:03:35.940
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: in the grant of the confidential expenses of the various agencies mentioned,

asr-005277
06:03:36.360 --> 06:03:41.100
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: but we will reserve those questions to the agencies that are in question.

asr-005278
06:03:41.540 --> 06:03:46.160
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: But nonetheless, Madam Speaker, good sponsor, the answer I'm hearing is that,

asr-005279
06:03:46.660 --> 06:03:53.160
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: yes, there were, there's proof, and nakita natin kung paano naabuso yung confidential expenses.

asr-005280
06:03:54.160 --> 06:03:58.880
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So, now we mitigated it by ensuring that in the next budget cycle,

asr-005281
06:03:59.220 --> 06:04:02.820
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: yung mga nararapat na lang yung pwedeng gastahan.

asr-005282
06:04:03.380 --> 06:04:08.220
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: But, Madam Speaker, good sponsor, am I interpreting it correctly that, right now,

asr-005283
06:04:08.520 --> 06:04:16.620
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: there is no mechanism to ensure non-abusive confidential fund spending

asr-005284
06:04:16.620 --> 06:04:23.480
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: other than by leaving it to COA when it receives its audit agency reports

asr-005285
06:04:23.480 --> 06:04:24.140
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: and submits it to the agency?

asr-005293
06:04:25.680 --> 06:04:34.020
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And to mitigate it in the next budget cycle when an anomaly has been discovered,

asr-005294
06:04:34.020 --> 06:04:36.180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: which can happen, you know, years later.

asr-005295
06:04:36.680 --> 06:04:42.260
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Are there no mechanisms in place that DBCC or the DBM can exercise

asr-005296
06:04:42.260 --> 06:04:45.360
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: other than what I've specified, Madam Speaker, good sponsor?

asr-005297
06:04:45.360 --> 06:04:54.020
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Madam Speaker, distinguished colleague, yes, the DBCC family recognizes that point,

asr-005298
06:04:54.160 --> 06:05:00.860
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: that at this point, there are, nandun lang po, nasa level lang po nang kuha.

asr-005299
06:05:01.260 --> 06:05:07.360
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: It's really like a post-audit arrangement in terms of CIF.

asr-005300
06:05:08.360 --> 06:05:10.480
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So, yun po, we recognize that point.

asr-005301
06:05:10.480 --> 06:05:15.340
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So, Madam Speaker, good sponsor, there are no preventive mechanisms in place

asr-005302
06:05:15.340 --> 06:05:18.640
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: in the existing rules, like in the 2015 Joint Circular,

asr-005303
06:05:19.060 --> 06:05:21.920
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: where questionable plans for spending can be halted,

asr-005304
06:05:21.980 --> 06:05:27.900
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: even though the Confidential Expenses Plan, or Annex A,

asr-005305
06:05:28.120 --> 06:05:34.140
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: is already attached when the request for allocation of confidential expenses

asr-005306
06:05:34.140 --> 06:05:37.340
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: is submitted to DBM, Madam Speaker, good sponsor.

asr-005308
06:06:15.340 --> 06:06:19.680
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Madam Speaker, distinguished colleague, upon conferring with DBM,

asr-005309
06:06:20.200 --> 06:06:25.640
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: so, the only thing that is submitted to them when the releases are requested

asr-005310
06:06:25.640 --> 06:06:28.440
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: is something like a physical and financial plan.

asr-005311
06:06:28.640 --> 06:06:33.900
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: And even the contents are very vague to the point that they're unable to detect

asr-005312
06:06:33.900 --> 06:06:39.660
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: at that stage whether there may be issues down the road.

asr-005313
06:06:39.660 --> 06:06:43.480
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So, admittedly po, because of the nature of the expenses themselves,

asr-005314
06:06:43.960 --> 06:06:45.120
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: naka-sealed envelope.

asr-005315
06:06:45.340 --> 06:06:48.480
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So, they're not able to validate it at that point.

asr-005316
06:06:48.680 --> 06:06:52.020
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So, on the part of DBM, during the SARA release,

asr-005317
06:06:52.460 --> 06:06:58.560
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: unfortunately, walang mechanism in place at the moment for them to be able to check.

asr-005318
06:06:58.660 --> 06:07:02.440
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So, it's really at the part of COA once they do the audit.

asr-005319
06:07:03.340 --> 06:07:04.860
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: Madam Speaker, good sponsor,

asr-005320
06:07:06.280 --> 06:07:09.620
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: so, essentially, we hope that COA does a good job.

asr-005321
06:07:09.620 --> 06:07:13.240
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: But at the end of the day, this means that there can be years

asr-005322
06:07:13.240 --> 06:07:14.620
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: wherein these disbursements,

asr-005323
06:07:15.340 --> 06:07:21.340
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: these disbursements happen at kung naspotan ng COA

asr-005324
06:07:21.340 --> 06:07:24.000
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: yung anomalous spending,

asr-005325
06:07:24.000 --> 06:07:27.200
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: dito lang po magsisimulang investigasyon

asr-005326
06:07:27.200 --> 06:07:31.860
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: at dito po magkakaroon ng chance na matignan

asr-005327
06:07:31.860 --> 06:07:35.100
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: at syempre yung pinakagusto nating mangyari, mabawi.

asr-005328
06:07:35.100 --> 06:07:38.800
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So, as it stands, Madam Speaker, good sponsor,

asr-005329
06:07:38.800 --> 06:07:45.140
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: not only does this representation see that confidential expenses, confidential funds,

asr-005330
06:07:45.340 --> 06:07:51.060
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: is not in line with our constitutional principles

asr-005331
06:07:51.060 --> 06:07:54.760
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: of accountability, of transparency,

asr-005332
06:07:55.340 --> 06:07:56.980
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: of full public disclosure,

asr-005333
06:07:57.700 --> 06:08:02.660
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: of all the state's transactions involving public interests.

asr-005334
06:08:02.860 --> 06:08:05.720
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: We also believe that confidential funds and expenses

asr-005335
06:08:05.720 --> 06:08:07.500
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: are a relic of opaque governance

asr-005336
06:08:07.500 --> 06:08:13.500
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: that has no place after the misspending of them has been exposed.

asr-005337
06:08:14.620 --> 06:08:15.180
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: The ongoing implications,

asr-005338
06:08:15.340 --> 06:08:19.300
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: the impeachment proceedings expose how billions in confidential appropriations

asr-005339
06:08:19.300 --> 06:08:22.880
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: were dispersed with zero real-time accountability,

asr-005340
06:08:22.880 --> 06:08:27.840
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: shielded by sealed envelopes and post-audits that take years to surface.

asr-005341
06:08:27.840 --> 06:08:31.060
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: And I think this is not a mere technical flaw.

asr-005342
06:08:31.060 --> 06:08:34.120
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: This can be a systemic weapon against the people's purse.

asr-005343
06:08:34.120 --> 06:08:39.140
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: We heard that there are moves to amend the rules.

asr-005344
06:08:39.140 --> 06:08:42.040
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: So while we're waiting for that,

asr-005345
06:08:42.040 --> 06:08:43.340
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: we're of the stance that there should be no confidential expenses.

asr-005348
06:08:45.660 --> 06:08:47.320
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: In this budget,

asr-005349
06:08:47.320 --> 06:08:49.560
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: and it should be allocated instead,

asr-005350
06:08:50.060 --> 06:08:52.280
Rep. Renee Louise M. Co: to different services that our people

asr-005351
06:08:52.280 --> 06:08:54.220
