asr-005696
06:42:13.000 --> 06:42:17.100
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: And 3.3 and down to 3.3% in 2028.

asr-005697
06:42:19.340 --> 06:42:20.020
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: Kasi,

asr-005698
06:42:20.180 --> 06:42:22.040
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: kaya ako lang ito,

asr-005699
06:42:22.300 --> 06:42:23.580
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: cause for concern,

asr-005700
06:42:24.680 --> 06:42:26.540
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: if we really look at it,

asr-005701
06:42:27.840 --> 06:42:30.000
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: for the second quarter 2026,

asr-005702
06:42:30.320 --> 06:42:32.880
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: real GDP growth was 2.3%.

asr-005703
06:42:32.880 --> 06:42:36.240
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: August inflation was 6.1%.

asr-005704
06:42:36.900 --> 06:42:41.440
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: Bottom 30% of household inflation was actually 8.2%.

asr-005705
06:42:41.440 --> 06:42:43.960
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: These are concerning data.

asr-005706
06:42:44.960 --> 06:42:47.080
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: Kung titignan talaga natin.

asr-005707
06:42:47.780 --> 06:42:49.340
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: Now, as I mentioned,

asr-005708
06:42:50.160 --> 06:42:51.020
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: we also feel it.

asr-005709
06:42:51.960 --> 06:42:55.200
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: Fuel prices alone is projected to go up to,

asr-005710
06:42:56.120 --> 06:43:01.540
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: diesel prices projected to go up to as high as 100 pesos per liter.

asr-005711
06:43:02.260 --> 06:43:03.800
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: That will have an economic impact.

asr-005712
06:43:03.800 --> 06:43:05.380
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: In fact, makikita nyo,

asr-005713
06:43:05.860 --> 06:43:06.060
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: mas,

asr-005714
06:43:06.060 --> 06:43:07.600
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: less traffic ngayon,

asr-005715
06:43:07.700 --> 06:43:09.680
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: especially yung mga public utility vehicles.

asr-005716
06:43:09.960 --> 06:43:10.180
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: They,

asr-005717
06:43:11.040 --> 06:43:12.840
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: not as much fly the roads anymore.

asr-005718
06:43:13.260 --> 06:43:13.580
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: Dahil,

asr-005719
06:43:14.080 --> 06:43:15.440
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: it's better to stay at home

asr-005720
06:43:15.440 --> 06:43:16.780
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: dan maglabas ka,

asr-005721
06:43:17.320 --> 06:43:19.480
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: bumiyahi ka dahil hindi ka kikita.

asr-005722
06:43:23.040 --> 06:43:23.960
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Mr. Speaker,

asr-005723
06:43:24.140 --> 06:43:25.300
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: my distinguished colleague,

asr-005724
06:43:25.780 --> 06:43:27.500
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: on the part of the economic managers,

asr-005725
06:43:27.940 --> 06:43:28.640
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: they assure,

asr-005726
06:43:29.200 --> 06:43:31.360
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: they give the assurance that they review

asr-005727
06:43:31.360 --> 06:43:34.600
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: these macroeconomic assumptions every three months po.

asr-005728
06:43:34.600 --> 06:43:35.920
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So, quarterly naman,

asr-005729
06:43:36.060 --> 06:43:40.520
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: depending on the realities that are prevailing,

asr-005730
06:43:40.680 --> 06:43:43.100
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: in-update naman po nila yung macroeconomic assumptions.

asr-005731
06:43:43.700 --> 06:43:44.180
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: Dahil,

asr-005732
06:43:44.900 --> 06:43:45.780
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: well, yung sakin lang,

asr-005733
06:43:45.900 --> 06:43:47.440
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: we have to look at the indicators.

asr-005734
06:43:48.560 --> 06:43:51.900
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: Is our economy already in its full capacity?

asr-005735
06:43:52.560 --> 06:43:53.800
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: Given the current rate,

asr-005736
06:43:53.860 --> 06:43:54.340
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: I believe,

asr-005737
06:43:55.800 --> 06:43:58.420
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: mahirap nang tumaas pa yan.

asr-005738
06:43:58.700 --> 06:43:59.660
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: And it will go down,

asr-005739
06:43:59.780 --> 06:44:00.720
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: given the current state.

asr-005740
06:44:01.280 --> 06:44:03.020
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: We're also looking at 2028.

asr-005741
06:44:03.940 --> 06:44:05.440
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: Anong ibig ko sabihin sa 2028?

asr-005742
06:44:06.060 --> 06:44:08.240
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: It's an election year.

asr-005743
06:44:09.380 --> 06:44:10.000
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: Investors,

asr-005744
06:44:10.180 --> 06:44:11.780
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: both foreign and local,

asr-005745
06:44:12.820 --> 06:44:13.280
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: usually,

asr-005746
06:44:13.800 --> 06:44:15.620
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: they hold on investments.

asr-005747
06:44:15.920 --> 06:44:17.640
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: Dahil, because of political uncertainty.

asr-005748
06:44:18.220 --> 06:44:19.620
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: That is also something that we

asr-005749
06:44:19.620 --> 06:44:21.060
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: have to consider.

asr-005750
06:44:21.880 --> 06:44:23.980
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: Madali magtaas nang magtaas ng budget

asr-005751
06:44:23.980 --> 06:44:26.060
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: pagka hindi natin pera yung ginagamit.

asr-005752
06:44:26.920 --> 06:44:28.320
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: Like in a company,

asr-005753
06:44:28.400 --> 06:44:29.260
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: when you run a company,

asr-005754
06:44:29.780 --> 06:44:32.960
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: you don't just like approve a huge budget

asr-005755
06:44:32.960 --> 06:44:34.580
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: if you know that it cannot be sustained.

asr-005756
06:44:34.940 --> 06:44:35.580
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: Kasi ang nararamdaman,

asr-005757
06:44:36.060 --> 06:44:40.220
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: we have to look at the state of our economy.

asr-005758
06:44:40.440 --> 06:44:41.640
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: It's already, as I mentioned,

asr-005759
06:44:41.860 --> 06:44:42.600
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: full capacity.

asr-005760
06:44:43.880 --> 06:44:44.040
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: Now,

asr-005761
06:44:45.080 --> 06:44:46.040
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: ang problema rin,

asr-005762
06:44:47.380 --> 06:44:48.080
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: as we all know,

asr-005763
06:44:48.160 --> 06:44:49.880
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: excess spending drives up inflation.

asr-005764
06:44:52.420 --> 06:44:52.620
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: So,

asr-005765
06:44:53.240 --> 06:44:56.300
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: kagaya ng sinabi ni Sheck Balizakan,

asr-005766
06:44:56.440 --> 06:44:56.820
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: alam mo naman,

asr-005767
06:44:57.240 --> 06:44:59.700
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: ang economy natin is consumption driven.

asr-005768
06:45:00.000 --> 06:45:03.700
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: It's not money coming from external sources.

asr-005769
06:45:03.980 --> 06:45:07.100
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: It's everyone's money just going around.

asr-005770
06:45:07.780 --> 06:45:10.740
Rep. Jesus "Bong" C. Suntay: So, well, these are my concerns.

asr-005771
06:45:11.160 --> 06:45:18.480
