Rep. JC M. Abalos: kaya hindi pa na ito turn over?

asr-006702
07:49:13.380 --> 07:49:15.600
Rep. JC M. Abalos: When? They could have said that during the budget

asr-006703
07:49:15.600 --> 07:49:16.660
Rep. JC M. Abalos: deliberations last year.

asr-006704
07:49:27.540 --> 07:49:37.660
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, we understand, Madam Speaker,

asr-006705
07:49:37.820 --> 07:49:40.240
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: the concern of our distinguished colleague.

asr-006706
07:49:40.840 --> 07:49:45.400
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Really, from the 2025 deliberations,

asr-006707
07:49:45.980 --> 07:49:48.980
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: it was really because of this requirement

asr-006708
07:49:48.980 --> 07:49:50.700
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: for the data privacy officers,

asr-006709
07:49:50.820 --> 07:49:53.920
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: which we thought would not be a hindrance

asr-006710
07:49:53.920 --> 07:49:57.320
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: to the full turnover of CBMS data.

asr-006711
07:49:58.000 --> 07:50:00.040
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: And that's the reason why

asr-006712
07:50:00.040 --> 07:50:02.180
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: at the time,

asr-006713
07:50:02.880 --> 07:50:04.860
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: the requirement wasn't

asr-006714
07:50:04.860 --> 07:50:06.900
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: fully implemented.

asr-006715
07:50:08.340 --> 07:50:08.860
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: And then,

asr-006716
07:50:10.240 --> 07:50:11.340
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: over the course of

asr-006717
07:50:11.340 --> 07:50:13.560
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: the turnover to the LGUs,

asr-006718
07:50:13.620 --> 07:50:14.660
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: it became a requirement.

asr-006719
07:50:14.960 --> 07:50:16.980
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Madam Speaker, ano po ang measured error rate

asr-006720
07:50:16.980 --> 07:50:18.000
Rep. JC M. Abalos: ng CBMS?

asr-006721
07:50:20.000 --> 07:50:21.040
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Ilan ang duplicate?

asr-006722
07:50:21.500 --> 07:50:22.420
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Ilan ang missing household?

asr-006723
07:50:23.200 --> 07:50:24.740
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Ilan ang maliang household composition?

asr-006724
07:50:25.320 --> 07:50:26.640
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Ilan maliang employment status?

asr-006725
07:50:26.640 --> 07:50:34.120
Rep. JC M. Abalos: ilan ang maling socioeconomic information, may mga tao ba sa database na sinasabing patay na pero buhay pa pala.

asr-006726
07:50:34.480 --> 07:50:42.320
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Gusto ko pong malaman dahil napaka-importante po nito habang pinaplano natin ang budget ng bawat departamento na umaasa sa datos.

asr-006727
07:50:42.740 --> 07:50:51.540
Rep. JC M. Abalos: At napaka-importante po, Madam Speaker ng CBMS, dahil isa po itong gabay para sigurado tayo na ang mga pulisiyan natin sinasalamin niya ang pangangailangan ng pamayanan.

asr-006728
07:50:56.640 --> 07:51:06.200
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Madam Speaker, so the CBMS is a census.

asr-006729
07:51:06.200 --> 07:51:13.420
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So after which the census is conducted, the PSA then checks with the death registry.

asr-006730
07:51:14.440 --> 07:51:21.500
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So that is the way in which we check at least for the deaths recorded.

asr-006731
07:51:23.760 --> 07:51:26.580
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, but in terms of the margin of error,

asr-006732
07:51:26.640 --> 07:51:40.440
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: it's really a continuous back-to-forth, I think it's a case-by-case basis regarding which constituency or which area, which jurisdiction would be subject to this.

asr-006733
07:51:40.440 --> 07:51:46.820
Rep. JC M. Abalos: So up to now, Madam Speaker, wala pa po tayong precise number kung ano yung margin of error dun sa mga datos na nakokolekta natin mula sa CBMS.

asr-006734
07:51:48.080 --> 07:51:56.500
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Wala po tayong error rate, wala po tayong metric or data sa mga kinokolekta natin kung mayroong erroneous na entry.

asr-006735
07:51:56.640 --> 07:51:57.840
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Wala po tayong idea.

asr-006736
07:52:00.460 --> 07:52:05.940
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, just to clarify, Madam Speaker, the CBMS is a census, it's not a survey.

asr-006737
07:52:06.800 --> 07:52:10.340
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So it's literally a collection of data.

asr-006738
07:52:11.060 --> 07:52:21.860
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Madam Speaker, pwede ko po ba malaman, ano yung pinakamatandang household record na ginagamit pa rin ngayon bilang current CBMS information?

asr-006739
07:52:21.860 --> 07:52:26.620
Rep. JC M. Abalos: For example, gusto ko po malaman, Madam Speaker, ano yung average or median age?

asr-006740
07:52:26.640 --> 07:52:34.100
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Considering na hindi naman siya ginawa all at once. May mga census kayong ginawa sa ibang time frame.

asr-006741
07:52:34.200 --> 07:52:38.280
Rep. JC M. Abalos: So pwede po ba namin malaman, Madam Speaker, ano yung average or median age ng records?

asr-006742
07:52:41.580 --> 07:52:49.820
Rep. JC M. Abalos: May mga records po ba tayo galing mula 2022, 2023, 2024, 2025, 2026? Pwede po ba namin malaman yun, Madam Speaker?

asr-006743
07:52:56.640 --> 07:53:19.920
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: 2024 CBMS, Madam Speaker, is the oldest record that we have for using for PSA data.

asr-006744
07:53:19.920 --> 07:53:25.040
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Ano naman po, Madam Speaker, yung pinakabago? 2024 lang ba lahat?

asr-006745
07:53:26.640 --> 07:53:44.460
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Kasi naiintindihan ko po, Madam Speaker, the first cycle, POPs and CBMS 2024, I want to find out if there are certain household information collected beyond 2024.

asr-006746
07:53:44.460 --> 07:53:50.460
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Let's say last year, may mga sinensos ba kayo ng 2025? May mga sinensos ba kayo ng 2026?

asr-006747
07:53:50.460 --> 07:53:57.060
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Or 2024 lang ba lahat?

asr-006748
07:53:57.460 --> 07:54:13.920
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: For social protection, Madam Speaker, the oldest would be 2024. But for the FIES, which is the Family Income and Expenditure Survey, it would be just for 2026.

asr-006749
07:54:14.440 --> 07:54:20.440
Rep. JC M. Abalos: So meron pong two-year interval yung FIES and for social protection.

asr-006750
07:54:20.460 --> 07:54:21.740
Rep. JC M. Abalos: For social services, is that correct?

asr-006751
07:54:22.060 --> 07:54:23.980
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, two-year interval, Madam Speaker.

asr-006752
07:54:24.600 --> 07:54:34.140
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Okay. So, Madam Speaker, yung tanong ko po sa PSA, and of course, for the guidance of all our government agencies who are relying on the CBMS data,

asr-006753
07:54:34.820 --> 07:54:40.840
Rep. JC M. Abalos: malaking pagkakaiba po kasi yung mga nakokollect natin ng 2026 and 2024.

asr-006754
07:54:41.520 --> 07:54:49.460
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Dahil sa isang household, in the span of two years, a lot can change. May mga nawawala ng trabaho, may mga lumilipat.

asr-006755
07:54:50.460 --> 07:55:01.580
Rep. JC M. Abalos: So, yung tanong po dito, masyado na bang luma ang household information, let's say, ng 2024 para gamitin sa beneficiary targeting?

asr-006756
07:55:01.960 --> 07:55:12.500
Rep. JC M. Abalos: And I also want to know, Madam Speaker, maglalaan tayo muli ng 5 billion para sa CBMS census, kailan po yung target date natin para isagawa ang second cycle?

asr-006757
07:55:20.460 --> 07:55:42.920
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, Madam Speaker.

asr-006758
07:55:42.920 --> 07:55:49.120
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Madam Speaker, the agency agrees that given the long interval,

asr-006759
07:55:50.460 --> 07:55:58.520
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: we can't fully capture the shocks that we experience over the course of those two years.

asr-006760
07:55:58.960 --> 07:56:09.940
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So, that's precisely the reason why for 2027, we're asking for 5 billion, because of the shocks that happened in 2025 and also, of course, 2026.

asr-006761
07:56:09.940 --> 07:56:17.540
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So, really, the 5 billion for the CBMS for 2027, besides the regular census processes,

asr-006762
07:56:20.460 --> 07:56:32.400
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: so, the effects of those shocks in 2025 and 2026, so that social protection programs and all social policies would be informed and tailored accordingly.

asr-006763
07:56:32.960 --> 07:56:37.300
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Madam Speaker, kailan po yung target natin para sa second cycle ng CBMS?

asr-006764
07:56:38.380 --> 07:56:40.540
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: September 2027, Madam Speaker.

asr-006765
07:56:40.960 --> 07:56:48.660
Rep. JC M. Abalos: And gusto ko po malaman, ano yung pinaka-recent na CBMS data turnover na ibinigay ng PSA sa LGU this year?

asr-006766
07:56:49.220 --> 07:56:50.300
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Ano yung pinaka-recent yung turnover?

asr-006769
07:57:30.000 --> 07:57:33.550
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: First quarter of 2026, Madam Speaker.

asr-006770
07:57:33.550 --> 07:57:52.800
Rep. JC M. Abalos: So you mean to tell me, Madam Speaker, kunwari isa po akong LGU, natanggap ko lamang ang aking CBMS data nung taong 2026, tapos 2027 maglalaan tayo ng 5 bilyon ulit, tapos kokolektahan na naman ako ng data sa 2027?

asr-006771
07:57:52.800 --> 07:57:59.180
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Hindi po ba, Madam Speaker, parang nakapanghinayang na isang taon lang halos napakinabangan ng data na na-collect?

asr-006772
07:57:59.640 --> 07:58:06.420
Rep. JC M. Abalos: And, since malapit na po matapos oras ko, Madam Speaker, may I just illustrate kung gaano po kaimportante ang CBMS?

asr-006773
07:58:06.560 --> 07:58:10.340
Rep. JC M. Abalos: And I hope our kind sponsor helps me verify this information.

asr-006774
07:58:11.200 --> 07:58:12.660
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Magbibigay po ako ng example.

asr-006775
07:58:13.440 --> 07:58:17.100
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Status of CBMS source, social pension validation.

asr-006776
07:58:17.400 --> 07:58:19.180
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Para po ito sa social pension ng ating mga seniors.

asr-006777
07:58:20.040 --> 07:58:21.100
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Total potential balance.

asr-006778
07:58:21.140 --> 07:58:23.020
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Beneficiaries identified from CBMS.

asr-006779
07:58:23.200 --> 07:58:24.080
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Batches 1 to 3.

asr-006780
07:58:24.460 --> 07:58:28.060
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Figure, 568,651.

asr-006781
07:58:28.600 --> 07:58:34.980
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Remaining for field validation, 251,318.

asr-006782
07:58:35.540 --> 07:58:41.780
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Madam Chair, sa aming pagsusuri, nagpapakita naman na gumagana mas kipapano ang ating CBMS.

asr-006783
07:58:41.900 --> 07:58:45.540
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Dahil may mga na-identify tayong mga beneficiaries.

asr-006784
07:58:46.240 --> 07:58:50.540
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Kaso lang po, binavalidate pa rin yung remaining 251,318.

asr-006785
07:58:51.140 --> 07:58:55.960
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Beneficiaries, hindi lamang po sa social pension for senior citizens.

asr-006786
07:58:56.460 --> 07:59:02.800
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Mas ka sa 4Ps, for example, may 107,000 households pa subject to validation.

asr-006787
07:59:03.420 --> 07:59:15.600
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Like I said, Madam Speaker, napakahalaga po ng CBMS dahil ito po ang listahan na pinapagbasihan natin for our social protection programs for our most vulnerable sectors.

asr-006788
07:59:15.600 --> 07:59:21.000
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Hindi po biro ang perang inilalaan natin para dito at napakahalaga po ito para mag-guide ang ating...

asr-006789
07:59:21.140 --> 07:59:22.460
Rep. JC M. Abalos: National Government Agency.

asr-006790
07:59:22.620 --> 07:59:24.840
Rep. JC M. Abalos: So, can we get a response from our distinguished sponsor?

asr-006791
07:59:26.460 --> 07:59:28.160
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Thank you, Madam Speaker.

asr-006792
07:59:28.840 --> 07:59:34.360
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: With regards to the social pension particularly, there are multiple layers of validation.

asr-006793
07:59:35.120 --> 07:59:40.120
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: For one, it's the PSA checks for the death registry.

asr-006794
07:59:40.580 --> 07:59:46.800
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: At the same time, given that there's an age requirement for being able to avail of the social pension, so 60,

asr-006795
07:59:47.000 --> 07:59:50.120
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: they also counter-check that with other surveys and other...

asr-006796
07:59:51.140 --> 07:59:51.640
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Registries.

asr-006797
07:59:52.400 --> 07:59:57.880
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So, that would be at least one of the reasons why validation takes so long.

asr-006798
07:59:58.940 --> 08:00:00.040
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: At least on the part of the...

asr-006799
08:00:00.000 --> 08:00:06.480
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Before I close, Madam Speaker, may I request from our distinguished sponsor as well as the PSA,

asr-006800
08:00:06.480 --> 08:00:14.340
Rep. JC M. Abalos: baka pwede niyo po ako bigyan ng timeline lang kung meron kayong target dates for completion sa mga bina-validate niyo pa pong population

asr-006801
08:00:14.340 --> 08:00:22.940
Rep. JC M. Abalos: dahil napakahalaga po yung timely delivery ng data, lalong-lalo na po na maglalaan tayo ulit ng mahigit 5 bilyong piso

asr-006802
08:00:22.940 --> 08:00:29.040
Rep. JC M. Abalos: at magsasagawa na naman tayo ng census sa parating na taon.

asr-006803
08:00:29.040 --> 08:00:37.820
Rep. JC M. Abalos: So, pwede ko po ba makuha yung commitment ng ating sponsor pati ng PSA na bibigyan tayo ng timeline kung kailan nila tatapusin ang validation,

asr-006804
08:00:38.120 --> 08:00:44.340
Rep. JC M. Abalos: hindi lamang sa social pension, hindi lamang sa 4Ps, kundi sa lahat ng programa na may pending pa tayong validation.

asr-006805
08:00:45.800 --> 08:00:52.580
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, Madam Speaker. The agency will assess and will furnish a copy to our good colleagues.

asr-006806
08:00:53.100 --> 08:00:58.580
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Madam Speaker, gusto ko pong ulitin and I hope hindi po ako mamisinterpret ng definition.

asr-006807
08:00:59.040 --> 08:01:11.320
Rep. JC M. Abalos: I want the CBMS to succeed. Napakaganda po kasi ng vision ng batas dahil napakahalaga na alam po natin kung saan may deprivation of services.

asr-006808
08:01:11.540 --> 08:01:17.140
Rep. JC M. Abalos: We must know where government resources must go to populations that need it the most.

asr-006809
08:01:17.640 --> 08:01:24.880
Rep. JC M. Abalos: And of course, magandang bigyan natin ang pagkakataon yung mga LGU na magplano based on actual household conditions.

asr-006810
08:01:25.880 --> 08:01:28.280
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Yun lamang po, Madam Speaker.

asr-006811
08:01:29.040 --> 08:01:34.540
Rep. JC M. Abalos: Salamat po ako sa ating distinguished sponsor, pati po sa DepDev at sa PSA. Maraming salamat po. Magandang gabi po.

asr-006812
08:01:34.800 --> 08:01:36.460
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Thank you, Madam Speaker.

asr-006813
08:01:36.660 --> 08:01:39.040
Deputy Speaker Maria Rachel J. Arenas: Thank you, Honorable Abalos, Majority Leader.

asr-006814
08:01:48.040 --> 08:01:57.560
Rep. Crispin Diego D. Remulla: Madam Speaker, I move that we recognize the Honorable Roberto Nazal of BH Party-list to interpellate on the proposed budget

asr-006815
08:01:57.560 --> 08:01:59.020
Rep. Crispin Diego D. Remulla: of the Department of Economy, Planning, and Development,

asr-006816
08:01:59.040 --> 08:02:03.160
Rep. Crispin Diego D. Remulla: including its attached agencies and corporations.

asr-006817
08:02:03.840 --> 08:02:07.700
Deputy Speaker Maria Rachel J. Arenas: The Honorable Roberto Nazal is recognized.

asr-006818
08:02:08.700 --> 08:02:12.920
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Thank you, Madam Chair, distinguished sponsor. Good evening to the DepDev.

asr-006819
08:02:15.500 --> 08:02:25.160
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Madam Chair, through you, do you agree, distinguished sponsor, that when government spending is significantly delayed

asr-006820
08:02:25.160 --> 08:02:27.720
Rep. Roberto Nazal: or falls short of program,

asr-006821
08:02:29.040 --> 08:02:30.520
Rep. Roberto Nazal: that can slow economic growth?

asr-006822
08:02:32.000 --> 08:02:34.460
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, Madam Speaker. We agree.

asr-006823
08:02:36.500 --> 08:02:42.300
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Every year, we have unobligated, unused, and reverted appropriations.

asr-006824
08:02:43.760 --> 08:02:47.500
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Does DepDev compute the economic cost?

asr-006825
08:02:48.620 --> 08:02:55.980
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Not just the unused money, but the projects, jobs, services, and economic activity that were delayed?

asr-006826
08:02:55.980 --> 08:02:56.080
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Thank you.

asr-006827
08:02:59.040 --> 08:03:14.540
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, Madam Speaker, there is a competition with regards to primary infrastructure,

asr-006828
08:03:14.720 --> 08:03:21.400
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: the effects of delays in primary infrastructure projects, and also social programs.

asr-006829
08:03:21.960 --> 08:03:22.300
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Madam Speaker.

asr-006830
08:03:22.300 --> 08:03:26.080
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Thank you for that, distinguished sponsor.

asr-006831
08:03:26.760 --> 08:03:27.300
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Madam Chair, and do you show the...

asr-006832
08:03:27.300 --> 08:03:28.500
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Madam Chair, and do you show the...

asr-006833
08:03:28.500 --> 08:03:31.760
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Madam Chair, and do you show this to the agencies concerned?

asr-006834
08:03:32.660 --> 08:03:36.340
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Does DepDev, minapakita po ba ito sa mga ahensya?

asr-006835
08:03:37.340 --> 08:03:43.340
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And do we tell them what their failure to implement is costing the economy?

asr-006836
08:03:47.600 --> 08:03:48.280
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Okay.

asr-006837
08:03:49.160 --> 08:03:50.560
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, Madam Speaker.

asr-006838
08:03:51.240 --> 08:03:53.200
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: These are discussed with the agencies.

asr-006839
08:03:53.480 --> 08:03:56.800
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: This is also reported to the President through the Economic Development Council.

asr-006840
08:03:56.800 --> 08:03:57.880
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Okay.

asr-006841
08:03:58.500 --> 08:04:01.120
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Thank you for that, distinguished sponsor.

asr-006842
08:04:02.420 --> 08:04:09.180
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Natsi-check po ba natin, distinguished sponsor, Madam Chair, kung ano yung bottlenecks?

asr-006843
08:04:09.180 --> 08:04:23.540
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And once identified, do we recommend what the executive and the legislature needs to do to help departments address them?

asr-006844
08:04:25.460 --> 08:04:26.760
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, these are checked, Madam Speaker.

asr-006845
08:04:28.500 --> 08:04:40.100
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, kapag may cabinet meeting po, do we flag the repeat underspenders and explain what their failure to implement is costing the economy?

asr-006846
08:04:41.820 --> 08:04:43.800
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Yes, Madam Speaker, the level of the cabinet.

asr-006847
08:04:43.800 --> 08:04:50.580
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Do we have the data kung sino po ang laging underspending?

asr-006848
08:04:51.440 --> 08:04:55.660
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And can you give a sample kung ano po ang nagiging cost nito sa economy?

asr-006849
08:04:56.660 --> 08:04:57.300
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Okay.

asr-006850
08:04:58.500 --> 08:05:19.500
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Madam Speaker, just for those that fall within the purview of the DEPDEV, which is the primary infrastructure programs and the social programs,

asr-006851
08:05:19.640 --> 08:05:24.220
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: but in terms of agency per agency, that would be under the DBM?

asr-006852
08:05:24.220 --> 08:05:28.220
Rep. Roberto Nazal: For example, in 2020...

asr-006853
