asr-007557
08:36:26.480 --> 08:36:28.120
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Just, almost done, ma'am.

asr-007558
08:36:28.960 --> 08:36:29.520
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Almost done.

asr-007559
08:36:30.120 --> 08:36:33.440
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, because I understand that deficits can make sense.

asr-007560
08:36:33.580 --> 08:36:35.400
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Kasi right now, we're deficit spending.

asr-007561
08:36:36.120 --> 08:36:39.500
Rep. Roberto Nazal: If we borrow for productive investments that generate growth,

asr-007562
08:36:39.760 --> 08:36:43.540
Rep. Roberto Nazal: but if we borrow and the money cannot be implemented effectively,

asr-007563
08:36:44.320 --> 08:36:47.020
Rep. Roberto Nazal: doesn't that weaken the justification for additional debt?

asr-007564
08:36:47.040 --> 08:36:49.060
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, yun po ang isa sa gusto kong tingnan.

asr-007565
08:36:49.780 --> 08:36:50.180
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Secondly,

asr-007566
08:36:51.120 --> 08:36:55.840
Rep. Roberto Nazal: has DEV-DEV modeled what level of deficit is actually optimal for the Philippines?

asr-007567
08:36:56.700 --> 08:37:02.220
Rep. Roberto Nazal: And what would it take eventually to balance the budget without damaging growth and essential services?

asr-007568
08:37:02.740 --> 08:37:04.840
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, wala po ba tayong long-term plan?

asr-007569
08:37:14.840 --> 08:37:21.100
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: Madam Speaker, the DEV-DEV is involved with at least the revisions and updating of the medium-term fiscal framework.

asr-007570
08:37:21.120 --> 08:37:26.900
Rep. Bella Vanessa B. Suansing: So, these are challenges and issues that the DEV-DEV also considers.

asr-007571
08:37:27.700 --> 08:37:28.920
Rep. Roberto Nazal: So, okay. Thank you.

asr-007572
08:37:29.020 --> 08:37:34.120
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Madam Chair, just a quick manifestation to end my interpolation.

asr-007573
08:37:35.500 --> 08:37:37.760
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Planning should not stop with setting targets.

asr-007574
08:37:38.720 --> 08:37:43.220
Rep. Roberto Nazal: For me, DEV-DEV should also know what is preventing government from implementing them,

asr-007575
08:37:44.200 --> 08:37:46.600
Rep. Roberto Nazal: what that failure costs the economy,

asr-007576
08:37:46.820 --> 08:37:49.240
Rep. Roberto Nazal: and what government needs to do to fix it.

asr-007577
08:37:49.800 --> 08:37:50.960
Rep. Roberto Nazal: Every decision,

asr-007578
08:37:50.960 --> 08:37:51.560
Rep. Roberto Nazal: to spend,

asr-007579
08:37:51.680 --> 08:37:52.220
Rep. Roberto Nazal: has a cost.

asr-007580
08:37:52.940 --> 08:37:54.700
Rep. Roberto Nazal: But every decision not to spend

asr-007581
08:37:54.700 --> 08:37:56.040
Rep. Roberto Nazal: or to delay spending

asr-007582
08:37:56.040 --> 08:37:57.580
Rep. Roberto Nazal: also has a cost.

asr-007583
08:37:58.200 --> 08:38:02.560
Rep. Roberto Nazal: I hope DEV-DEV will be much more proactive in monitoring the spending

asr-007584
08:38:02.560 --> 08:38:06.120
Rep. Roberto Nazal: and implementation performance of our agencies,

asr-007585
08:38:06.840 --> 08:38:08.520
Rep. Roberto Nazal: identifying bottlenecks early

asr-007586
08:38:08.520 --> 08:38:11.240
Rep. Roberto Nazal: and recommending to both the Executive and Congress

asr-007587
08:38:11.240 --> 08:38:12.480
Rep. Roberto Nazal: what needs to be done

asr-007588
08:38:12.480 --> 08:38:16.020
Rep. Roberto Nazal: before these problems translate into slower growth.

asr-007589
08:38:16.360 --> 08:38:17.100
